; xfail: wrong number of arguments for Sink.emit: got 0, expected 1
;
; A method call that passes FEWER arguments than the method declares must be
; a hard planner diagnostic. It used to plan clean: lookup_method# only
; consults method_params_match# (the one place that compares argument COUNT)
; when a receiver has SEVERAL same-named methods; a single by-name candidate
; was taken unconditionally. The emitter then builds the call type from the
; argument VALUES, so llc accepted it too, and the callee read whatever the
; ABI register still held.
;
; That is not a theoretical hole. dazzle's FotSink called
; TeXFOTBuilder.start_line_field() one argument short and produced CORRECT
; output at -O0 — the caller's own `nic` happened to still sit in x1 — then
; silently dropped a line-field break priority once `opt -O2` reallocated the
; register (2026-08-01). tools/arity-audit.py catches the same class in
; already-emitted IR; this catches it at plan time.

define Sink()
{
    function emit(this: pointer[Sink], value: int) returns int
    {
        value
    }
}

function main() returns int
{
    var s Sink()
    return s.emit()
}
